! **Eight atoms and a cell under 500 kbar.** The conventional cubic cell of
! diamond silicon -- a supercell of the primitive one, which P28a established is
! a regime rather than a size -- compressed by an applied pressure and relaxed
! back with `calculation = 'vc-relax'`.
!
! What it adds over the two-atom arsenic of QE's own `pw_vc-relax` cases is
! everything that scales with the cell: eight atoms whose forces and nine cell
! coordinates share one Hessian, a structure factor that vanishes *exactly* at
! the G-vectors the cubic cell's exact fractions kill (P28a's `abs` trap, whose
! consumer here is the stress rather than the second derivative), and a
! neighbour list large enough that an image lost to compression is a real term
! rather than an erfc tail below the comparison floor.
!
! `celldm(1) = 10.20` is silicon's zero-pressure lattice constant to within what
! this functional relaxes it to (10.19 with `Si.pz-vbc`), so the whole of the
! trajectory is the response to the pressure.
!
! **100 kbar and not 500, because 500 closes the gap.** At 500 kbar this cell
! compresses by 25%, diamond silicon becomes metallic, and a run with the default
! fixed occupations is then not a calculation at all: `pw.x` relaxes happily in
! the frozen basis and then reports `convergence NOT achieved after 100
! iterations` in its final SCF at the relaxed cell, while pypresso converges the
! same ill-posed problem to a fixed-occupation solution 7.3e-3 Ry away. Two codes
! disagreeing about a system neither should be describing is not a test. At 100
! kbar the cell moves ~9%, which is as much as the arsenic cases move, and the
! crystal stays an insulator on both sides.
!
! Cubic symmetry survives the trajectory, so the relaxed cell must still be
! cubic. Nothing imposes it -- `cell_dofree` is `'all'`, so every entry of `h`
! is free to move -- which makes the off-diagonal entries returning to zero a
! check on the symmetrised stress that shares nothing with `pw.x`.
 &control
    calculation = 'vc-relax'
    tprnfor = .true.
    tstress = .true.
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 1
    celldm(1) = 10.20
    nat = 8
    ntyp = 1
    ecutwfc = 24.0
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
 &ions
 /
 &cell
    cell_dynamics = 'bfgs'
    press = 100.0
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si  28.086  Si.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS crystal
 Si 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Si 0.00 0.50 0.50
 Si 0.50 0.00 0.50
 Si 0.50 0.50 0.00
 Si 0.25 0.25 0.25
 Si 0.25 0.75 0.75
 Si 0.75 0.25 0.75
 Si 0.75 0.75 0.25
K_POINTS automatic
 4 4 4 0 0 0
